  "season": null,
  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Thieboudienne (also spelled ceebu jen) means rice and fish in Wolof. It was inscribed on UNESCO's list of intangible cultural heritage in 2021. The dish originated in Saint-Louis in northern Senegal.",
