        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend parsley, 2 garlic cloves and green chilli to a paste. Push into slits cut across the fish and into the belly. Season the fish with salt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a large heavy pot over high heat. Fry fish for 3 minutes per side until golden. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the same oil, fry sliced onion for 5 minutes. Add remaining garlic and cook 1 minute. Add tomato puree and cook 2 minutes. Add blended tomato and onion. Cook for 20 minutes until sauce is deep red and oil floats."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add carrots and cabbage wedges to the sauce. Pour in 800ml water. Simmer for 20 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the vegetables and most of the broth. Add rinsed rice to the pot with just enough broth to cover by 2cm. Bring to a boil, then cover tightly and cook on lowest heat for 25 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove lid. Increase heat to medium for 5 minutes to form the xoon crust. Return fish and vegetables to rest on top, cover for 5 minutes, then serve."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Rice is undercooked",
              "cause": "Not enough broth or heat too low",
              "fix": "Add 100ml hot broth, replace lid, and cook for a further 10 minutes. Resist lifting the lid in the first 20 minutes."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Fish falling apart",
              "cause": "Overcooked or not sturdy enough",
              "fix": "Use the thickest fillets available. Cook fish briefly at the start; it finishes cooking when returned to the pot at the end."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thieboudienne is cooked every day across Senegal, typically at midday as the main meal. It is a communal dish, served in a single large platter shared by everyone at the table. The dish reached UNESCO intangible heritage status in 2021, the first Senegalese dish to receive the designation. Variations exist across the coast: some versions use smoked fish, others add fermented shellfish (guedj) for depth."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}